NODE_ENV=test
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://lectra:replace-me@127.0.0.1:55432/lectra_dev
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://lectra:replace-me@127.0.0.1:55432/lectra_test
ALLOW_TEST_DATABASE=lectra_test
# Foundation suite additionally requires ALLOW_FOUNDATION_TESTS to match this database.
# Seeding additionally requires SEED_SYNTHETIC_DATA to match this database and
# SEED_OWNER_PASSWORD / SEED_RESPONDENT_PASSWORD supplied privately (12–128 code points).
# No passwords are supplied by this example. Never seed a development/deployed database.
# Other isolated suites require their corresponding opt-in to match a NEW database:
# ALLOW_FEATURE_TESTS=lectra_test
# ALLOW_RELEASE_TESTS=lectra_test
# ALLOW_POST_RELEASE_TESTS=lectra_test
# ALLOW_BROWSER_TESTS=lectra_test
# ALLOW_CLOUD_TESTS=lectra_test
# Browser tests also require DEVELOPMENT_DATABASE_URL distinct from TEST_DATABASE_URL,
# DATABASE_URL=TEST_DATABASE_URL, APP_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:4174 and a private SESSION_SECRET.
# RESTART_PASSWORD must match the private feature-suite seed password for restart checks.
